    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Competitive Dialogue allows bidders to submit initial solutions after being successful at the selection stage. It allows you to negotiate proposed solutions with bidders. This may help to open up cross-border markets by encouraging bidders to discuss possible solutions.",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Quickfire Guide",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Competitive Dialogue may be beneficial where:",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "greater flexibility is needed - for example, highly complex and risky projects",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "greater flexibility is needed - for example, highly complex and risky projects",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "you are procuring innovative projects",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "you are procuring innovative projects",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "you are unable to specify your requirements e.g. your technical, financial or legal solutions. Therefore bidders may have a major role in defining the solution",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "you are unable to specify your requirements e.g. your technical, financial or legal solutions. Therefore bidders may have a major role in defining the solution",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "you cannot assess without in-depth dialogue on what the market can offer",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "you cannot assess without in-depth dialogue on what the market can offer",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "the Open or Restricted Procedures may not deliver the expected outcomes.",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "the Open or Restricted Procedures may not deliver the expected outcomes.",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You cannot use this procedure when your requirements can be provided by many different market operators, or it is an off-the-shelf service or supply.",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The use of Competitive Dialogue must always be justified, although there is no need to include that justification in your Contract Notice. Unlike the Competitive Procedure with Negotiation, here the specification requirements concentrate on your organisation's needs without having to detail the nature, characteristics or solutions to be offered.",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Please Note",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland."
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00019",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue",
      "ordinal": 19,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00020",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Advantages of Competitive Dialogue are:",
      "ordinal": 20,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00021",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "it allows organisations to clarify, specify or optimise the final bids",
      "ordinal": 21,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00022",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "your negotiations with your ultimate preferred bidder may also confirm financial commitments or other terms contained in the tender to finalise the contract. This helps, for example, in situations where a preferred bidder needs to secure final planning permission for a project before the contract can be concluded.",
      "ordinal": 22,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00023",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Care should be taken before selecting this route:",
      "ordinal": 23,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00024",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "you must ensure that you legally satisfy the criteria of using Competitive Dialogue",
      "ordinal": 24,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00025",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "you should be aware that this process is costly and resource intensive for you and bidders",
      "ordinal": 25,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00026",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "this procedure is likely to result in a significant increase in procurement timescales.",
      "ordinal": 26,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "In all cases \"days\" are calendar days and not working days. The final day must however be a working day in Scotland.",
        "The Pros and Cons of a Competitive Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00027",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
      "ordinal": 27,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00028",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "A Competitive Dialogue has several stages. These are detailed below:",
      "ordinal": 28,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00029",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings",
      "ordinal": 29,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00030",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You should publish your minimum requirements, award criteria and their weightings. These cannot be changed during the negotiation process.",
      "ordinal": 30,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00031",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "If your process will be conducted in successive stages, this must be stated in the Co ntract Notice or descriptive document .",
      "ordinal": 31,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00032",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The day after the Contract Notice is sent for publication, at least 30 days must elapse before the closing date for receipt of selection stage information.",
      "ordinal": 32,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00033",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Note that after this stage there are no further set minimum timescales for submissions, however timescales must be reasonable. When fixing time limits, you must take account of the complexity of the contract and the time required for writing bids. You must set out an indicative timeframe in the Contract Notice and/or a descriptive document.",
      "ordinal": 33,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00034",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You must allow any bidder to submit a request to participate in response to a Contract Notice within the time limit set.",
      "ordinal": 34,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "1. Publish Minimum Requirements, Award Criteria and their Weightings"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00035",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Invite Selected Candidates to Participate",
      "ordinal": 35,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "2. Invite Selected Candidates to Participate"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00036",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You then invite the selected candidates to participate in the dialogue, using an Invitation to Take Part in Dialogue (ITPD). There is no minimum period specified for bids in response to this document, but it must be reasonable.",
      "ordinal": 36,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "2. Invite Selected Candidates to Participate"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00037",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You may limit the number of suitable bidders who meet your selection criteria to be invited to participate in the procedure. You should invite at least three bidders (if three or more meet selection criteria) to the dialogue process in order to ensure genuine competition.",
      "ordinal": 37,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "2. Invite Selected Candidates to Participate"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00038",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Bidders do not submit tenders before starting dialogue with your Organisation.",
      "ordinal": 38,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "2. Invite Selected Candidates to Participate"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00039",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Negotiations/Dialogue",
      "ordinal": 39,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00040",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Following this initial response, you may decide to have several stages of negotiations/dialogue in order to develop solutions and reduce the number of solutions (if indicated in the contract notice or the descriptive document).",
      "ordinal": 40,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00041",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "If there are successive stages, you must ensure that in the final stage the number of solutions remaining make for genuine competition. This means there must be enough solutions or qualified bidders.",
      "ordinal": 41,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00042",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You can decide on the number of dialogue stages.",
      "ordinal": 42,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00043",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You may reduce the number of bidders by applying the award criteria to suppliers’ proposals during multiple dialogue stages before using the criteria again to assess bidders’ final bids.",
      "ordinal": 43,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00044",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "During the dialogue, Organisations must ensure equal treatment of all participants.",
      "ordinal": 44,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00045",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Any clarifications, specification, optimisation, additional information or negotiations must not involve changes to the essential aspects of the tender. You must not provide information in a discriminatory manner which may give any bidder an advantage over others.",
      "ordinal": 45,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "3. Negotiations/Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00046",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "4. Conclusion of Dialogue",
      "ordinal": 46,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "4. Conclusion of Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00047",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You must inform all bidders when the dialogue is being concluded.",
      "ordinal": 47,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "4. Conclusion of Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00048",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You must invite each remaining bidder to submit their final tender on the basis of the solution(s) presented and specified during the dialogue.",
      "ordinal": 48,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "4. Conclusion of Dialogue"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00049",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "5. Deadline for Receipt of Final Tenders",
      "ordinal": 49,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "5. Deadline for Receipt of Final Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00050",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "After the Invitations to Submit Final Tenders are sent out, you must set a deadline for receipt of final tenders. There is no minimum period specified but these must be proportionate by taking into account the contract complexity and the time required to prepare and submit a bid.",
      "ordinal": 50,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "5. Deadline for Receipt of Final Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00051",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You must extend the time limits for the receipt of tenders so that all bidders concerned are aware of all of the information needed to produce tenders e.g. where additional information has been requested by a supplier in good time and is not supplied at least six days before the time limit fixed for the receipt of tenders, or where there are significant changes made to the procurement documents.",
      "ordinal": 51,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "5. Deadline for Receipt of Final Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00052",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The length of extension must be proportionate to the importance of the information or change.",
      "ordinal": 52,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "5. Deadline for Receipt of Final Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00053",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "6. Contract Award",
      "ordinal": 53,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "6. Contract Award"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00054",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Final tenders may be further clarified before award of the contract, but this must not involve the essential aspects, cause discrimination, or distort competition. You apply the award criteria to assess bidders’ final bids and award the contract.",
      "ordinal": 54,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "6. Contract Award"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00055",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Care and Support Services",
      "ordinal": 55,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Care and Support Services"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00056",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "For many care and support services contracts, an organisation may use the procurement procedures, tools and techniques of its choosing. You should follow a procurement procedure, as a matter of best practice, that is proportionate to the value of the contract and to take account of some fundamental considerations (for example, the P rinciples of Procurement and Fair Work Practices ).",
      "ordinal": 56,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Care and Support Services"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00057",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "When doing so, you may choose to adapt or streamline the Competitive Dialogue procedure described in the Public Contracts (Scotland) Regulations 2015 . If you do so, you are not obliged to follow the detailed procedural requirements set out in those Regulations. You should therefore not refer to the Regulations in the tender documentation issued to participants, as this may create an expectation that the detailed procedural requirements will be followed. In all cases, you should ensure that the procurement process is described accurately and clearly and then adhered to.",
      "ordinal": 57,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Care and Support Services"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00058",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders",
      "ordinal": 58,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00059",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You can use Competitive Dialogue where all of the submissions you have received for an Open or Restricted Procedure are classed as either irregular or unacceptable.",
      "ordinal": 59,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00060",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "A tender is irregular where:",
      "ordinal": 60,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00061",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "it does not comply with the Procurement Documents",
      "ordinal": 61,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00062",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "it was received late",
      "ordinal": 62,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00063",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "there is evidence of collusion or corruption",
      "ordinal": 63,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00064",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "it has been found by you to be abnormally low",
      "ordinal": 64,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00065",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "A tender is unacceptable where:",
      "ordinal": 65,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00066",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "it was submitted by a bidder that does not have the required qualifications; or",
      "ordinal": 66,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00067",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "the price tendered exceeds your Organisation’s budget (as determined and documented before the Procurement Procedure started.",
      "ordinal": 67,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Irregular and Unacceptable Tenders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00068",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Variants",
      "ordinal": 68,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00069",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You may authorise or require variant bids. However this must be specified in the Contract Notice.",
      "ordinal": 69,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00070",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Your Procurement Documents must set out the minimum requirements and how the variant will be evaluated. Variants cannot be considered unless:",
      "ordinal": 70,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00071",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "they are specified within your Procurement Documents",
      "ordinal": 71,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00072",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "they are linked to the subject matter of the contract",
      "ordinal": 72,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00073",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "they meet the minimum requirements.",
      "ordinal": 73,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00074",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "All variant bids should be evaluated using the same criteria as the standard bids and compared on a like-for-like basis.",
      "ordinal": 74,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00075",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You should also consider whether to allow potential bidders to offer different TUPE scenario options within their bids. If so, you must provide clear directions to bidders to ensure that bids are compared on a like-for-like basis.",
      "ordinal": 75,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Variants"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00076",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Issuing Documents",
      "ordinal": 76,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00077",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Invitation to Submit a Final Tender is a procurement document that can only be finalised in the course of the actual dialogue. As a result it does not need to be made available at the same time as the Contract Notice.",
      "ordinal": 77,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00078",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The procurement documentation relevant to the first part of the procedure (up to and including the Invitation to Take part in Dialogue (ITPDs) must be made available:",
      "ordinal": 78,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00079",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "through the internet",
      "ordinal": 79,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00080",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "for free",
      "ordinal": 80,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00081",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "simultaneously",
      "ordinal": 81,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00082",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "by electronic means",
      "ordinal": 82,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00083",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "include all ITT documents (unless exclusions apply, for example confidentiality) when the Contract Notice is published. In such cases another, non-internet method must be used to provide the information.",
      "ordinal": 83,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Issuing Documents"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00084",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Principles of Procurement",
      "ordinal": 84,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Principles of Procurement"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00085",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "T he activities you undertake at this stage must be carried out in a carefully managed manner that supports the Principles of Procurement .",
      "ordinal": 85,
      "heading_path": [
        "When to Use Competitive Dialogue",
        "Please Note",
        "Competitive Dialogue Stages and Timescales",
        "Principles of Procurement"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    }
